1 NAME BHRIGU
2 GIVN BHRIGU
2 NICK Bhrigu The Guru
1 SEX M
1 OCCU Brahma Rishi
1 TITL Saptarishi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maharishi Bhrigu was one of the seven great sages, one of the Saptarshis in ancient India, one of many Prajapatis (the facilitators of Creation) created by Brahma (The God of Creation) [1], the first compiler of pr
2 CONC edictive astrology, and also the author of Bhrigu Samhita, the astrological (Jyotish) classic written during the Vedic period, Treta yuga
2 CONT
2 CONT Maharishi Bhrigu (Sanskrit: भृगु ) was one of the seven great sages, the Saptarshis सप्तऋषि  , one of the many Prajapatis (the facilitators of Creation) created by Brahma. The first compiler of predictive astrology, and also the a
2 CONC uthor of Bhrigu Samhita, the astrological (Jyotish) classic. 
2 CONT
2 CONT भ्रां भक्तैक रक्षी च भृगु: पाताभ्रभ्रंशनः ।  
2 CONT
2 CONT मुनीनामुत्तमाचार्य: श्रीभृगुः शरणं मम ।।
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhraam Bhaktaik Rakshee Cha Bhriguhu Patabhrabhranshanah !Muneenaamuttamaachaaryah Shree Bhriguhu Sharanam Mama !!
2 CONT
2 CONT Maharshi Bhrigu is one of the brightest and most illumined among the ten great sons of the Brahma – the God of creation. He is a famous Vedic Seer and many vedic hymns are attributed to him. He has played a vital role in the compi
2 CONC lation of “Atharva Veda”. Since the very beginning, he has been engaged in the welfare of humanity through his famous book “Bhrigu Samhita”. 
2 CONT
2 CONT My note- So in Brighu’s period also compilation was there
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhrigu is considered a Manasa Putra ("mind-born-son") of Brahma. The adjectival form of the name, Bhargava, is used to refer to the descendants and the school of Bhrigu. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Manusmriti, Bhrigu was a compatriot of and lived during the time of Manu, the Hindu progenitor of humanity. Bhrigu had his Ashram (Hermitage) on the Vadhusar River, a tributary of the Drishadwati River near Dhosi Hill
2 CONC  in the Vedic state of Brahmavarta, presently on the border of Haryana and Rajasthan. Along with Manu, Bhrigu had made important contributions to Manusmriti, which was constituted out of a sermon to a congregation of saints in the
2 CONC  state of Brahmavarta, after the great floods in this area, nearly 10,000 years ago. As per Skanda Purana, Bhrigu migrated to Bhrigukutch, modern Bharuch on the banks of the Narmada river in Gujarat, leaving his son Chyavana at Dh
2 CONC osi Hill.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Khyati, one of the nine daughters of sage Kardama.  Shrukracharya, Chyavana, Dhata and Vidhata are his famous sons and Sree – Lakshmi, his daughter. Maharshi Markandeya, Maharshi Aurva, Maharshi Jamdagni and Bhag
2 CONC wan Parshurama –  have brought laurels to his clan and were great Rishis in their own right. Bhagwan Dattatreya is said to be his Master. One of his descendants was sage Jamadagni, who in turn was the father of sage Parashurama, c
2 CONC onsidered an avatar of Vishnu.              
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhrigu finds mention in Shiva Purana and Vayu Purana, where he is shown present during the great yajna of Daksha Prajapati (his father-in-law).
2 CONT
2 CONT He supports the continuation of the Daksha yajna even after being warned that without an offering for Shiva, it was asking for a catastrophe for everyone present there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In Tattiriya Upanishad, he had conversation with his father Varuni on Brahman.
2 CONT
2 CONT भृ॑गु॒र्वै वा॑रु॒णिः । वरु॑णं॒ पित॑र॒मुप॑ससार ।
2 CONT
2 CONT अधी॑हि भगवो॒ ब्रह्मेति॑ । तस्मा॑ ए॒तत्प्रो॑वाच ।
2 CONT
2 CONT अन्नं॑ प्रा॒णं चक्षुः॒ श्रोत्रं॒ मनो॒ वाच॒मिति॑ ।
2 CONT
2 CONT तꣳहो॑वाच । यतो॒ वा इ॒मानि॒ भूता॑नि॒ जाय॑न्ते ।
2 CONT
2 CONT येन॒ जाता॑नि॒ जीव॑न्ति ।
2 CONT
2 CONT यत्प्रय॑न्त्य॒भिसंवि॑शन्ति । तद्विजि॑ज्ञासस्व । तद्ब्रह्मेति॑ ।
2 CONT
2 CONT स तपो॑ऽतप्यत । स तप॑स्त॒प्त्वा ॥ १
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhrigu, the son of Varuna, went near his father and said, "Godman, teach me Brahman." To him, he said this, "Food, breath, eye, ear, mind, speech." He said (further), "That from which these beings are born, that by which, when bor
2 CONC n, these beings live, that into which they enter upon departing, That you should know, That is Brahman.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Bhagavad Gītā, Krishna says that among sages, Bhrigu is representative of the opulence (ostentatiously rich and superior in quality). of God (Chapter- X/25) and the same thought has found has its echo in the Eleventh Canto 
2 CONC of the Bhagawatam. 
2 CONT
2 CONT महर्षीणां भृगुरहं गिरामस्म्येकमक्षरम् |
2 CONT
2 CONT यज्ञानां जपयज्ञोऽस्मि स्थावराणां हिमालय: || 25||
2 CONT
2 CONT maharṣhīṇāṁ bhṛigur ahaṁ girām asmyekam akṣharam
2 CONT
2 CONT yajñānāṁ japa-yajño ’smi sthāvarāṇāṁ himālayaḥ
2 CONT
2 CONT I am Bhrigu amongst the great seers and the transcendental Om amongst sounds. Amongst chants know me to be the repetition of the Holy Name; amongst immovable things I am the Himalayas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patience test of Trimurti (Tenth Canto of the Bhagawatam)
2 CONT
2 CONT Many great sages gathered at the bank of the river Sarasvati to participate in Maha Yagya. All the great saints and sages could not decide that out of the Trinity Lord Vishnu, Brahma, and Shiva who is pre-eminent and to whom shoul
2 CONC d they offer Pradhanta(प्रधानता) (Master) of that Yagya. With the consent of all the great saints presents there, it was decided that Bhrigu will test and decide who was pre-eminent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon being entrusted with the task, Maharishi Bhrigu decided to test each of the Trimurtis. Being ignored and attacked by Lord Brahma and Lord Shiva, he visited Lord Vishnu. Vishnu was asleep and Bhrigu kicked him in the chest to 
2 CONC wake him up, as Bhrigu was enraged by the fact that Vishnu always keep on resting on Shesha . Vishnu smilingly welcomed Bhrigu who realised his egotistical outbursts with extreme pain. He begged for forgiveness and Vishnu forgave 
2 CONC him. He then declares Vishnu the greatest among Trimurti. But Lakshmi was angry with Bhrigu and cursed the Brahmans that they would achieve wealth only by hard work.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhrigu and Places associated with him
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhrigu's Ashram 'Deepotsaka' was located at the base of Dhosi Hill in present-day village Dhosi on the border of Narnaul district in Haryana and Jhunjunu district of Rajasthan, from where he migrated to Bharuch. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Chyavana, known for Chyavanprash also had his Ashram at Dhosi Hill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhrigu is also worshipped at Bharuch, Swamimalai, Tirumala, Ballia, Nanguneri,Thiruneermalai, Mannargudi.
2 CONT
2 CONT My note- Naguneri is near Valliyur in between Nagerkovil and Tirunelveli
2 CONT
2 CONT An Ashram for Bhrigu is in Maruderi, Kanchipuram district in Tamil Nadu. Khedbrahma in Gujarat is associated with Brahma and Bhrigu 's legend of testing Trinity. Lastly, Bhrigu migrated to Bhuinj Satara, Maharashtra where he took 
2 CONC Samadhi. His ashram and his daughter's Laxmi's temple also situated there. His sons chyavan's ashram and samadhi are also situated on chyavaneshwar hill near Bhuinj.         
2 CONT
2 CONT  In Taittriya Upanishad (तैत्तिरीय उपनिषद्)first six anuvakas of Bhrigu Valli are called Bhargavi Varuni Vidya, which means "the knowledge Bhrigu got from (his father) Varuni". It is in these anuvakas that sage Varuni advises Bhri
2 CONC gu with one of the oft-cited definition of Brahman, as "that from which beings originate, through which they live, and in which they re-enter after death, explore that because that is Brahman". This thematic, all encompassing, ete
2 CONC rnal nature of reality and existence develops as the basis for Bhrigu's emphasis on introspection and inwardization, to help peel off the outer husks of knowledge, in order to reach and realize the innermost kernel of spiritual Se
2 CONC lf-knowledge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhrigu Samhita (भृगु संहिता)
2 CONT
2 CONT After the incident of testing of the trinity, Bhrigu decided to write his famous books of astrology, the Bhrigu Samhita. Maharishi Bhrigu collected birth charts, wrote full-life predictions and compiled them together as Bhrigu Sam
2 CONC hita. Bhrigu Samhita is believed to be one of the first book of its kind in the field of astrology.
2 CONT
2 CONT My note- So astrology was there from the period of sage Brighu.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Every year 10th May is celebrated as BHRIGU JAyanti महर्षि भृगु जयंती.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is train maned after BHRIGU Train No 22427/28 Bhrigu SF Express(Northern Railway) weekly train runs between ANAND VIHAR(NEW DELHI) and BALLIA (UP).
2 CONT
2 CONT The train is named after Bhrigu. At BALLIA Thousands of Rishies are said to have performed puja here. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bhrigu Mandir is a temple in Ballia (142 kms fromVARANASI)
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a  Maharishi Bhrigu Foundation established at Haridwar(Uttarakhand).
2 CONT
2 CONT Chakshusa Manvantara..
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Matsya Purana, sage Manu was the first man (and the first human) created by God. In the above Purana it was mentioned that Lord Brahma created, using his divine powers, the Goddess Shatrupa (as Saraswati was first
2 CONC  called) and out of the union of Brahma and Shatrupa was born Manu.
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 Manvantaras together form a day of Brahma.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 14 Manvantaras are Svayambhuva, Svarocisa, Uttama, Tamasa, Raivata, Caksusu, Vaivasvata, Savarni, Daksha-Savarni, Bramha-Savarni, Dharma-Savarni, Rudra-Savarni, Ruchi-Savarni and Bhouma-Savarni.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1      Manus of the current kalpa
2 CONT
2 CONT 1...1  First Manvantara – the interval of Swayambhu Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.2   Second Manvantara – the interval of Swarochisha Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.3   Third Manvantara – the interval of Uttama Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.4   Fourth Manvantara – the interval of Tapasa/Tamasa Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.5   Fifth Manvantara – the interval of Raivata Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.6   Sixth Manvantara – the interval of Chakshusha Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.7   The current, Seventh Manvantara – the interval of Vaivasvata Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.8   Eighth Manvantara – Surya Savarni Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.9   Ninth – Daksa Savarni Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.10 Tenth – Brahma Savarni Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.11 Eleventh – Dharma Savarni Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.12 Twelfth – Rudra Savarni Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.13 Thirteenth – Raucya or Deva Savarni Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.14 Fourteenth – Indra Savarni Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Vedic texts, current age of Brahma is 50 Brahma years and 1 brahma day (we are in the 1st day of 2nd half of brahma)and we are in the seventh "manvantara", in the 28th turnover of its 71 yuga cycles. In this cycle
2 CONC , we are in the start Kali Yuga.Chakshusha Manvantara is the sixth Manvantara. This Manvantar derived its name from Chakshush Manu.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sixth Manvantara – the interval of Chakshusha Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT SUDYUMNAN SEES RUDRA AND PARVATI
2 CONT
2 CONT Saptarshis list: Sumedhas, Virajas, Havishmat, Uttama, Madhu, Abhináman, and Sahishnnu. In Chakshusha-manvantara, Lord Vishnu's avatar was called Ajita.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ajita came as Chakshsusa Manu, the son of the demigod Chakshu. He had many sons, headed by Puru, Purusa and Sudyumna. During the reign of Chakshusa Manu, the King of heaven was known as Mantradruma. Among the demigods were the Apy
2 CONC as, and among the great sages were Havisman and Viraka.
2 CONT
2 CONT The current, Seventh Manvantara – the interval of Vaivasvata Manu
2 CONT
2 CONT Saptarshis list: Kashyapa, Atri, Vashista, Angira, Gautama, Agastya, Bharadvaja. During Vaivasvata-manvantara, Lord Vishnu's avatar is called Matsya.The seventh Manu, who is the son of Vivasvan, is known as Sraddhadeva(or satyavra
2 CONC ta ) or Vaivasvat(son of Vivasvan). He has ten sons, named Ikshvaku, Nabhaga, Dhrsta, Saryati, Narisyanta, Dista (Nabhanedista), Tarusa (Karusha), Prsadhra and Vasuman (Pramshu). In this manvantara, or reign of Manu, among the dem
2 CONC igods are the Adityas, Vasus, Rudras, Visvedevas, Maruts, Asvini-kumaras and Rbhus. The king of heaven, Indra, is known as Purandara, and the seven sages are known as Kashyapa, Atri, Vashista, Angira, Gautama, Agastya and Bharadwa
2 CONC ja.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
