1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In Hindu mythology, Durvasa (दुर्वास in Devanagari or durvāsa in IAST, pronounced [d̪urʋɑːsɐ] in classical Sanskrit), or Durvasas, was an ancient sage, the son of Atri and Anasuya. He is supposed to be an incarnati
2 CONC on of Shiva.[1][2][3][4][5] He is known for his short temper. 
