1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Janaka (Sanskrit: जनक, IAST: Janaka) is the King of Videha who ruled from Mithila, in the Hindu epic Ramayana. Janaka was married to Sunayana. He is the father of Sita and Urmila in the epic.[1] The term Janaka was
2 CONC  also the title adopted by all the kings of Videha, who were the descendants of the King Nimi and his son King Mithi. The King Mithi is considered as the first King of Videha who was titled with the term Janaka.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janaka
2 CONT
2 CONT Janaka, originally named Sīradhvaja, was born to King Hrasvaroman of Mithila and his wife Keikasi. 
