1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Madri - Second Wife of Pandu माद्री Madri was the sister of Salya, the king of Madhra. She became the second wife of Pandu, the King of the Kurus. She bore him the twins Nakula and Sahadeva, who were born by the gr
2 CONC ace of the Ashwini twins.
2 CONT
2 CONT When her husband died as a result of approaching her with amorous intent (this was due to a curse of a Rishi), she was heartbroken. After entrusting her children to Kunti, Pandu's other wife, she committed suicide on the funeral p
2 CONC yre of her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT On his way to Hastinapur, King Pandu encountered the army of Shalya, King of Madra. Very soon, Pandu and Shalya became friends and Shalya gave his only sister, Madri to Pandu, as a gift of their friendship. Looking at her beauty, 
2 CONC Pandu accepted the lady willingly and took her to Hastinapur.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT She is princes of Madra
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Madri
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Mahabharata epic, Madri, also called Madhuri, was sister of Shalya and princess of the Madra Kingdom who married Pandu and had two sons called Nakula and Sahadeva. The word Mādrī means 'she who is the princess of Madra king
2 CONC dom'.[37][better source needed] She was like a younger sister to Kunti. After Pandu was cursed by Rishi Kindama, Kunti and Madri accompanied him to the forest. There, using the mantra Rishi Durvasa gave Kunti, Madri gave birth to 
2 CONC Nakul and Sahadeva. Pandu was captivated by the beauty of Madri. King Pandu could not resist himself from touching Madri. And after that the curse that Pandu received before came true and Pandu died. Madri burnt herself on Pandu's
2 CONC  funeral pyre after handing over her children to Kunti.
2 CONT
2 CONT
