2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandhatri#cite_note-5  Mandhatri or Mandhata ](Sanskrit: मान्धातृ, Māndhātṛ), in Hindu mythology, was an Ikshvaku dynasty king and son of Yuvanashva.[1] The hymn 134 of the tenth mandala of the Rigve
2 CONC da is attributed to him.[2] He married Bindumati Chaitrarathi, daughter of Yadava king Shashabindu and granddaughter of Chitraratha.[3] According to the Puranas, he had three sons, Purukutsa, Ambarisha and Muchukunda.[4] According
2 CONC  to the Mahabharata, he was a son of the Suryavansha king Yuvanshva.[5]
