1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ugrasena''' (Sanskrit: उग्रसेन) is a Yadava king in Mahabharata epic. He was the king of Mathura, a kingdom that was established by the powerful Vrishni tribes from Yaduvanshi clan. Lord Krishna was the grandson
2 CONC  of Ugrasena. He established his grandfather as the ruler of Mathura again after defeating his uncle, King Kansa who was a wicked ruler. Before this, King Ugrasena was overthrown from power by his own son Kansa and was sentenced t
2 CONC o prison along with his niece Devaki and nephew in law Vasudeva to prison. Devki and Vasudev were parents of Lord Krishna.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT *Title	King
2 CONT *Affiliation	Yadava dynasty
2 CONT *Spouse	Padmavati
2 CONT *Children	Kansa, Devaki
2 CONT *Relatives	Ahuka (father)
2 CONT *Nationality	Kingdom of Mathura
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugrasena
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Vasudeva was the father of Lord Krishna. Devaki , daughter of the Yadava chieftain Ugrasena and sister of Kamsa was his mother. Please note that Krishna's father was called Vasudeva (with Va pronounced as V-uh). Krishna was called
2 CONC  Vasudeva ( with Va pronounced as Vaa) , which indicated his father's name (Vaasudeva means "of Vasudeva" per Sanskrit rules).May 17, 2015
