1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I was a Javanese prince of the Royal Family of the Majapahit. As a dignitary of the Kingdom of Singasari, I might have gone as the Royal Envoy of the Kingdom of Singasari to China (Yuan dynasty) on a diplomatic exp
2 CONC edition in 1325 (as some historians believe, he is the envoy whom a Chinese source calls Sengk'ia-lie-yu-lan).
2 CONT
2 CONT I served the King Kertanagara of Singasari. In 1286 I brought a Bodhisattva statue of Amoghapasa Lokesvara, which was a gift from my Lord Kertanagara of Singasari, to his vassal Srimat Tribhuwanaraja Mauli Warmadewa, the King of t
2 CONC he Kingdom of Dharmasraya. Later on I would marry his daughter. Our son founded the Minangkabau Kingdom on Sumatra.
