2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Maulana Hasanuddin (also spelled Hasanuddin) was a ruler of the Banten Sultanate from c. 1552 to 1570. Hasanuddin was a Azmatkhani Ba 'Alawi Sayyid, the son of Sunan Gunungjati and Nyai Ratu Kawunganten.
2 CONT
2 CONT He extended the domains of Banten to the pepper-producing region of Lampung, in South Sumatra. This area, which already had long-standing ties with West Java, facilitated Banten's rise to prominence as a pepper port.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT  M.C. Ricklefs, A History of Modern Indonesia Since c. 1300, 2nd ed., Stanford: Stanford University Press, 1994, p. 38
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT -
2 CONT Sultan of Banten
2 CONT ca. 1552–1570	Succeeded by
2 CONT Maulana Yusuf of Banten
2 CONT
2 CONT
